    <td>
<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Ultima Online 2 - UO2 Vault Dev Team Chat for 9/27/2000</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>[Gasper]</b> I'd like to welcome everyone to this month's chat with the Origin Dev Team and thank you for coming
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> And also thank the Dev Team for taking the time to spend time with the fans
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> To ask a question, we will have three people taking submissions
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> Those three will be Big_D, Elysium and Ghosty
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> To ask a question, just type "/msg name question" where name is who you want to submit it to and question is your question
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> You may start submitting questions to those three now and Cynthe has some introductions to do so take it away Cynthe!
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> Thanks for coming!  These are always fun. ;)  With so much coolness coming online every day, we wanted to introduce a couple new programmers... or rather, let them introduce themselves.  be nice to them... they've been crunching so much they've forgotten what the real sun looks like. :)
<br><b>[MrRiley]</b> Hello, I am a new server programmer for the Origin team.
<br>* Ubiq claps and applauds.
<br><b>[Exsanguinator]</b> Howdy folks, I'm a new addition to the game programming team.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> W00t!  Did I just say that?
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> Hello all, thanks for coming.  I am the new user interface programmer.
<br><b>[glyph]</b> Hi; I'm a new game programmer as well.
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> talkative, aren't they?  heehee... programmers
<br><b>[Medwynd]</b> brief and too the point :)
<br><b>[MrRiley]</b> I was the server lead on Segasoft's 10Six MMPG until recently
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> Okay, and here we go and remember, message Big_D, Elysium and Ghosty with your questions, not the members of the Dev Team :)
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Bushwa]</b> Will NPC Teachers tell you all of the skills they can teach when asked, or only the skills you are eligible to be taught?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Good question!
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We have many, many skills, and some teachers will know quite a few of them, so...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> To make your life easier, they will only tell you what you are able to learn.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[James|Orion|bruno]</b> We know that Ether is the opposite of Necromancy, but what exactly IS Ether Magic?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Essentially, it's goody-two shoes magic.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Not that I'm confirming the existence of Ether or necromancy, mind you, but if we were to have either one of them, that's what ether magic would be.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> =p
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Are there seasonal effects?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We have some pretty cool seasons.  We're still debating whether to have them affect you in a material way.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> You should see the screen shots the programmers have been passing around this week :)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Bushwa]</b> Are there any plans to allow mages to cast powerful spells (outside the ability of a single Mage) as a group by combining their power (mana)?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We have some plans to encourage group and sidekick casting.  Our focus isn't on rituals, as much as on 'combos'
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> or interactions between spells and abilities that make each other stronger.  
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Rituals have some messy problems and the end result isn't as cool as what we have - we think =)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Zurren]</b> will there be any sort of spell research system? or will it just be more like UO/EQ, in you have spells available at X level. If so, how will the spells differ between players? or will we all be "clone mages?"
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> There's no spell research, we've got the magic skill tree instead...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Fortunately the magic skill tree is really big...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Its got 10 unique schools..
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> More than any one player will be able to learn...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> If you want to get the most powerful spells in a given school...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Don't expect to be learning much from others...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Or if you want to dabble, you could learn a handful from several different magic schools..
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> So I think there'll be plenty of variation to keep all mages from being alike...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> even if they decide to spend all of their advancement in the magic skill tree.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Shike]</b> Will the whole skill tree be known to the public (a.k.a. Tree charts with manual) or will we as players have to find out whats out there?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Hmm...well, since teachers will only tell you what you are able to learn, if we didn't provide some sort of documentation, we'd
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> essentially be forcing a whole group of players to be trailblazers...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And since you can unlearn skills, this would not be all bad.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> However-
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> In the interests of not frustrating people, yeah, we'll let you know what is available.  Maybe not ALL of it :)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> But most of it.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[TWD]</b> Approximately how many cities will there be in Origins?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Oy.  Um...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Lots.  We have...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Around 8 major cities...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And many many many towns.
<br>* Ubiq watches Windfeather count his fingers and toes.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And even more - uh - I'm counting hairs now.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Hamlets :)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> The world is quite large.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Niobe]</b> can you give us an example how the character races may affect certain professions?
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Races affect professions in two ways...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> First of all, each race gets cost reductions to certain skill trees...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Therefore a Meer specializing in certain magic schools is going to get farther a little more quickly...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> than say a human...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Furthermore, there are also skils that are unique to a certain race...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> For example, Humans have access to Iolo's Deadly Crossbow Aiming...
