<br><b>[Mobius]</b> We've got a whole variey of technological weapons that I can guarantee you haven't seen before.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Er, yeah, I was working on death last week with the mo-cap guy.  He's crazy.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Shaar]</b> What will happen when I go to the wild lands and start killing everyone I see?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I will pull my hair amd say, 'I thought they would be nice to each other!'
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Hmm.  Well, you will get away with it at first.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Then, the system will say 'Hey, you're up to no good..'
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And it will then make it very, very easy for other people to lop off your arms, your legs, and your head.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And then...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> If you do it again, the system will say 'He's at it again!' as soon as you start.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And you'll lose more bits (and experience, since you get a debt when you die).
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Sanctum-Cair]</b> Will there be good looking character models in UO2? Look at AC, people are just plain ugly in that, and in EQ where people look good you also look like everyone else.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Yes, I can safely say our character models will look good.  Trust me.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> They are *quite* attractive.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[TiffanyCo_M]</b> Is posting bugs on public forums going to b an violation of conduct code? and resulting in account banning?
<br><b>[Vaxhacker]</b> Cloud room!
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Hyperion sometimes stares at them for hours.
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> Being someone who doesn't actually work on the game, but gets to just see the results, I'm always really blown away by the faces.
<br><b>[Thumper]</b> Malimn - Ghosty
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> <b></b>Tiffany]</b> Here's a hint: Tyrant will be running our Customer Support.
<br><b>[Ghosty]</b> Send your questions to me
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Zero tolerance is the only real way to run one of these games.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Tiffany: Gosh, I sure hope so :)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b>  <b>[Astalder]</b> How flexible will UO2 be upon entering beta, if players bring up a serious complaint, will you consider changing it, even if it means setting back the time of release?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Fairly flexible, within limits.  Our architecture will allow us to make changes to the balance and ruleset quite easily.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> (It's one of those benefits of experience that we talked about before).
<br><b>[Vaxhacker]</b> Data driven = good.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That being said, we do eventually have to ship, and we do have the ability to improve the game after launch as well.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> I don't anticipate this game being 'done' before ship - but then I don't anticipate it being 'done' for years and years.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> There are ALWAYS ways you can make these games bigger, better and cooler, and our architecture was designed to allow the live team to do just that.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Drac]</b> Whats the status on servers or worlds?  If you have seperate worlds will charachters be migratable?
<br><b>[Vaxhacker]</b> We will have multiple independent shards, just like UO does, for a variety of reasons.
<br><b>[Vaxhacker]</b> As far as character migration goes, that's not been decided.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Zeo-Sanctum]</b> Tried but True Question, Can you give a little more detail on what spells need regs?
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Low level spells in the primary magic schools require no reagents...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> As you go up in spell power, however, the reagent costs get greater and greater.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b>  <b>[Tchrin]</b> At ship will there be shards in Europe, or anywhere else outside the US?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We are doing all we can to ensure that the game will be localized and prepared for worldwide shards beforehand.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Will we have a simultaneous launch?  Too soon to tell.  
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Funes]</b> Will there be an allegiance system like in Asheron's Call?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We've done some preliminary design (theoretical stuff) about something like a political structure, BUT...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We are waiting to see how factions pan out in a couple of other games - UO among them - before we even think about taking more steps in that direction.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I'll be part of a roundtable on that next month.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Stay tuned to the Origin site :)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Rico]</b> Will there be a way to view the sky, to say look at the constellations and not have your avatar in the view?
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> We are experimenting with several different view modes for the camera. It's too early to rule out the possibility of 1st PPOV,
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> but there should be plenty of ways to gaze up at the sky.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[Niobe]</b> ROGUES!!! Are you looking into ways for 'evil' RPers to be able to effectively RP their professional roles while balancing the the risks and rewards? (ie no uber or nerfed thieves)?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Good question.  I like playing a rogue, myself.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I would like nothing better than 'Thief Online'
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We do have stealing and associated skills in the game...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> However, we have to balance that system so you can't just go out and steal your fellow adventurers dry without any fear of consequence.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> It's gotta be balanced like any other system, risk-reward...plus take into account the fact that stealing angers many people.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> So...yep, there will be penalties.  But it will be in the game :)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b>  <b>[Gonj]</b> Will I be able to brew my own Beer in the game? And if I get some really exotic hops from the wild lands, will it boost my drunken fighting?
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Yes, we do have brewing in the game. And yes we do have some drunken fighting. :)
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> When monsters kill a pc do they get experience and become stronger?
<br><b>[Exsanguinator]</b> we currently have the ability to give xp's to monsters...that system is in.
<br><b>[Exsanguinator]</b> as for whether or not they'll get stronger...that's a game balance issue to be decided.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Monsters are characters are NPCs are monsters are characters are NPCs...our programmers are awesome.
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> <b>[ViPeRdAeM0n]</b> Do they have hooded robes in uo2?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Of course we'll have hoods.  Trust me, none of the other developers wants to look at Windy's face, even in-game.
<br><b>[Ghosty]</b> Ewww.
<br>* Ubiq grins.
<br><br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I'm not going to say something now that will get me in trouble with Cynthe.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Thanks everyone for coming out.  We're actually doing great over here, lots of cool systems have come online in UWOOland
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That have really reminded me that we're working on the coolest game in the universe.  Hopefully next time around, we'll have
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> even more to talk about.  And as for those of you lucky enough to come to the UOFaire, can't wait to meet you and hear what you 
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Think of what we're doing so far!
<br><br><b>[Gasper]</b> Thanks to everyone for coming and thanks to the Dev Team for taking time out of their schedules to be with us tonight
<br><b>[Gasper]</b> We now return you to the previously scheduled program...already in progress.

</font>

</td></tr></table>

